# Keep build contexts free of host-only artefacts.
#
# Two of these are load-bearing rather than tidiness: a host `.venv` carries
# macOS binaries that are useless (and large) inside a Linux image, and a stale
# `__pycache__` makes pytest inside the container report HOST file paths.
#
# The `**/` prefix matters — Docker's ignore patterns are anchored at the
# context root, so a bare `__pycache__/` would only match one at the top level.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
